<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-Comalco 9 mth aluminium output rises.</title>
<headline>RTRS-Comalco 9 mth aluminium output rises.</headline>
<dateline>MELBOURNE 1996-10-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Comalco Ltd said on Thursday its primary aluminium output rose to 347,867 tonnes in the nine months to September 30 from 327,040 a year earlier after a rise in third quarter output to 122,390 tonnes from 109,955.</p>
<p>Comalco said the higher production was due to a higher number of cells operating at its Bell Bay smelter and increased line current on existing cells and new cells coming on line as part of the upgrade of the Tiwai Point smelter in New Zealand.  </p>
<p>Comalco also said its sales of aluminium rose to 344,127 tonnes in the nine months from 314,681 a year earlier and third quarter sales to 120,593 tonnes from 107,910 a year earlier.</p>
<p>The sales increase was due to the extra metal production and timing of shipments, it said. Comalco is owned 67 percent by RTZ Corp Plc-CRA Ltd.</p>
